|name3 = Festive New Year Neneko
}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''New Year Neneko''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Festive New Year Neneko''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
==='''Normal/Evolved Form'''===
This Neneko variant, much like the others and [[Neneko (Super Rare Cat)|the original]], specializes in metal enemies, offering an unreliable option to deal with the weaker ones for an incredibly low price. She differs from Neneko in that she gains Area Attack at the cost of 90 less range, plus she lacks the defining cat combo [[Sister Act (Combo)|Sister Act]]. This puts her at a great disadvantage, even more so than her other variants due to range being the only thing keeping them safe from most typical [[:Category:Metal Enemies|Metal]] enemies. On the other hand, her ability to crit with Area Attacks is incredibly rare, resulting in her being likely one of the best options against large numbers of Metal Doges or similarly weak peons. As with all Neneko variants, she is not meant to be and should not be used for non-metals.

==='''True Form'''===
Her multi-hit gives her more chances to crit, with each hit being as powerful as a full attack from her previous forms, at the cost of some attack speed. Combined with her faster cooldown, she improves noticeably. She can now more reliably deal with the likes of [[Metal Doge]]s and [[Metal One Horn]]s, but her fragility and low damage still keep her from being a powerful asset against tougher metal enemies.

{{Job|Classification = Critter}}

